#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This is the baseline example for the impaired driver study.
#
#Variants of this example decrease the preview time and increase the input delay. Shortening the preview time reflects the impaired driver's difficulty in processing visual information which is further away. Increasing the input delay models how the impaired driver can be slower to act, even when they have processed the path and decided how much to steer.
#
# All results are overlaid here for comparison purposes.
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

